-- RDX0123: an operator used that this file never declared — plan 90.
--
-- The lexer scans every spelling in `ASSIGNABLE_OPERATORS` whether or not a
-- file declares one, which is what let plan 90 ship without the pre-pass its
-- §1.3 priced. The consequence is that the boundary is the **parser's**, and
-- §1.5 wanted it loud: a diagnostic at the use site, naming the operator,
-- rather than a silently different program.
combined : u32 -> u32 -> u32
combined a b = a <+> b
